  "📦 Items": "",
  "📦 [b]Publishing a Reusable Asset Pack[/b]\nShare your custom 3D models, audio or code scripts with other map makers as a Workshop item.\n\n[b]Build a playground:[/b] turn the pack into a map where players can preview your models and try the systems you are sharing.\n\n[b]It stays out of the map library:[/b] the item is marked as an asset pack, so players browsing maps do not see it as a game to play, and the editor lists it wherever assets are imported from.\n\n[b]Easy importing:[/b] once a player has a copy, they import assets from it into their own maps in the editor.\n\n[b]Credit:[/b] imported files keep their author metadata, so the map that imports them credits you automatically.": "",
  "🔒 Unlock": "",
  "🔓 Lock": "",
  "🗑️ Delete": "",
  "🚀 [b]Publishing Your Map[/b]\nYour map is uploaded to the Steam Workshop under your own account. Nothing is reviewed by Realm first, and there is no waiting list: the item exists as soon as the upload finishes.\n\n[b]Who can see it:[/b] you choose the item's visibility on Steam. A public item appears in the in-game map library once Steam has it; a friends-only or private one is still playable by anyone you hand it to, and by players you host for.\n\n[b]Updating it:[/b] publishing again updates the same item in place, so subscribers receive the new version. If you rename the map, a new item is created instead, because the item is found by its name.\n\n[b]Playing it before you publish:[/b] use Test Map to play it straight out of this workspace, and host a lobby with it to play with other people. Neither step needs the Workshop.\n\n[b]Credit:[/b] the Workshop item's owner is the author of record, and the map's manifest lists the maps and assets it was built from so their creators are credited in game.": "",
